```

| File | Allowed contents |
| ---- | ---------------- |
| `modules/*/*.tsx` | Single page/screen |
| `modules/*/components/*.tsx` | Module-specific colocated UI |
| `components/*/*.tsx` | Single reusable cross-module component |
| `hooks/*.ts` | Single hook |
| `stores/*.store.ts` | Single Zustand store |
| `app/App.tsx` | Screen switch + providers only |

## State management

| Store | Purpose |
| ----- | ------- |
| `ui.store` | Current screen, selected game, library filters, import toast |
| `theme.store` | Active theme, custom theme list, CSS variable application |
| `session.store` | Active `GameSession` mirror from Tauri |

Server state (games list) uses TanStack Query in `useGames.ts` with invalidation after mutations.

## Tauri integration

All commands wrapped in `src/lib/tauri.ts`:

```typescript
export async function listGames(): Promise<Game[]> {
  return run<Game[]>('list_games')
}
```

`run()` checks `isTauriRuntime()` — falls back to `mockInvoke` in browser dev.

When adding a command: update Rust handler → register in `lib.rs` → add wrapper + types in frontend.

## Controller system

1. `GamepadManager` polls `navigator.getGamepads()`.
2. `ControllerMapping` maps button indices → `ControllerAction` (family-aware).
3. `useControllerNavigation` dispatches actions to `ui.store` (navigate, confirm, back, edit, add, section switch).
4. `FocusManager` maintains spatial focus graph; `Focusable` registers focusable elements.

Keyboard equivalents handled in the same hook.

## Testing

### E2E (Playwright)

```bash
yarn dev          # or yarn tauri:dev
yarn test:e2e
```

Home artwork, contrast, and route regressions live in `e2e/home-backdrop.spec.ts` and `e2e/macos-theme.spec.ts`.

### Typecheck

```bash
yarn run typecheck
```

Add Playwright coverage for new screens and controller flows. Bug fixes should include a regression spec when feasible.

## Dev workflow

| Command | Purpose |
| ------- | ------- |
| `yarn tauri:dev` | Full desktop app |
| `yarn dev` | Frontend only + mock API (faster UI iteration) |
| `yarn test:e2e:ui` | Debug Playwright interactively |

Browser dev sets theme via `localStorage.setItem('orbit.themeId', 'orbit')` in E2E boot helper.


Library offers All games, Orbit, and Connected views. Search starts with the full
collection and filters imported titles and cached GameHub titles by title or source.
Connected cards show GameHub status and keep provider actions separate from launching
an imported game. The shared GameHub query refreshes the visible download status.

`useBackdropTransition` keeps at most two backdrop layers in the shell. The browser decodes the incoming image before showing it, ignores late results after selection changes, and caches up to 24 lighting samples. Local artwork can use the Rust lighting command. The webview compositor runs the fades.


Glass surfaces share the material loaded by `GlassMaterialBootstrap`. They use
compositor blur with a Rust-generated texture and do not allocate canvas maps or
subscribe to panel geometry. Browser preview uses the same CSS without the native
grain texture. Translucent cards, buttons, badges, and fields use the same shared material through `orbit-panel` and `orbit-glass-control`.

Keyboard routing lives in `controllers/keyboard.ts`. Backspace has no navigation binding. Global navigation shortcuts yield to input, textarea, select, editable-content, textbox and combobox contexts, consumed events, composition, and system modifier combinations. Escape remains Back outside editing contexts. Dialogs handle Escape locally and preserve IME composition.


Theme cards use `ThemeCardArtwork` with a fixed 2:1 header. Backgrounds cover the
frame; logos remain contained within an inset box. Native sessions use one
streaming thumbnail batch, cached across navigation by TanStack Query. Browser
preview uses the packaged thumbnails generated with the same renderer.
`ArtworkImage` requests asynchronous decoding, keeps a shimmer until decoding
completes, fades the image in, handles errors, and ignores stale decode callbacks.
Reduced Motion disables shimmer and fade. No image decode or resize loop runs in
React rendering.

`useNavigationInput` mirrors input modality onto the document root in O(1) without
rerendering every card. Shared inset outlines cover spatial focus across routes
and body portals. Pointer movement, rather than layout-induced mouse enter,
switches back to pointer navigation.

Theme settings reuse the hydrated catalog and packaged previews. Native custom
entries provide runtime-only thumbnail paths; grids never need embedded image
blobs. Preview caches are separate from portable theme JSON. Concurrent catalog
requests share one promise, including StrictMode bootstrap effects. Theme grouping
uses a single O(n) map pass instead of copying the growing groups on each item.
